A numeric input between − and + steppers that formats its value.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/number-field)

<%= embed UI::NumberFieldPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
NumberField(default_value: 1, min: 0, max: 10, name: "quantity", aria_label: "Quantity")
NumberField(default_value: 19.99, step: 0.5, format: { style: "currency", currency: "USD" }, name: "price")
```

The visible input is a text field (`role="spinbutton"`) that shows the formatted value; a hidden input submits the
plain number under `name:`. It accepts typed numbers in the current locale's format and re-formats them on commit
(blur, Enter, a step). The steppers repeat while held and disable at a bound. Label it with a `<label for>` pointing
at its `id:`, a Field, or `aria_label:`.

